        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bun bo Hue has a more complex broth than pho. Lemongrass goes in whole and perfumes the stock over 3 hours. A finishing chilli oil infused with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "annatto-oil"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "annatto"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " gives the broth its red colour. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mam-ruoc"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "shrimp paste"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is added at the very end, just before serving, and is used with a careful hand."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "round-rice-noodles"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "round rice noodles"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " if you can find them. They have more chew than the flat noodles used in pho and stand up better to the heavily seasoned broth."
          }
        ]
      },
